    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1108">

                <pb facs="0830" n="754" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg754"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/206</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Silliman
                        to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Querétaro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-25T19:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 25, 1916, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s January 21, 5 p.m. Compañia Petrolera Maritima. Have had two
                    interviews with Foreign Secretary on this matter and <pb facs="0831" n="755"
                        xml:id="pg755"/> have gone over with him most carefully and fully the
                    Department’s message. The Secretary, speaking for General Carranza, limits
                    himself for the present to the following reply: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Government of Mexico is surprised that the Government of the United
                            States should make the representation transmitted when only the
                            interests of Mexican citizens appear concerned.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
